--- Rosetta Code: Sealed classes and methods
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sealed_classes_and_methods
--- Crow has no classes, no inheritance and no methods: a record (struct) is a fixed list
--- of fields, and functions are free functions. So every record is sealed — nothing can
--- extend it: a record that "is a" Parent and more is a record of its own, or one holding a
--- Parent as a field (composition), and a record's fields are only those it declares
--- (making one takes every field, and reading one it does not declare is refused before
--- the program runs). Nothing can be overridden either: a core builtin's name is reserved
--- (`fn len[x]` is refused), a standard module's names are reserved where it is imported
--- bare, and a module of the program's own is reached only through its prefix, so a
--- function the importer writes under the same name is another function, and the module's
--- own calls still reach its own.
--- What stays open is the other way round: a function reads fields, not kinds, so one
--- written for a Parent takes any record that has the fields it reads (each kind gets its
--- own compiled copy). To seal it to Parent, it asks the record's kind with type[], as the
--- Wren entry does — here only conditionally, as there: a Child under 15 is turned away.

struct Parent [name, age]

--- not a subclass: a record of its own that happens to have the same fields
struct Child [name, age]

--- composition, the one way to build on a record: a Teacher holds a Parent record
struct Teacher [person, school]

fn watch_movie[p]
    if type[p] ne 'Parent' and p.age lt 15
        log['Sorry, `p.name`, you are too young to watch the movie.']
    else
        log['`p.name` is watching the movie...']

watch_movie[Parent['Donald', 42]]
watch_movie[Child['Lisa', 18]]
watch_movie[Child['Fred', 10]]

--- a function over parents is handed the field
maria = Teacher[Parent['Maria', 35], 'Elm Street School']
watch_movie[maria.person]
log['`maria.person.name` teaches at `maria.school` (a `type[maria]` holding a `type[maria.person]`)']
